I fetched the 1.5.7-18 sources and read `Native.load` in `com.github.luben.zstd.util.Native`. I did not run the build, so the failing operation itself is unconfirmed.

`Native.load` first tries `System.loadLibrary("zstd-jni-<version>")`. If that fails, it opens the jar resource `/linux/<arch>/libzstd-jni-<version>.so`, copies it to a temp file, and calls `System.load`. Native Image supports all of this: resource inclusion and JNI registration are the kind of thing reachability metadata covers. Nothing here defines classes at runtime, uses an agent or substitution, or loads classes from outside the image. Because the failure is repairable, I did not take the `skip_unsupported` path.
